<p>Magnetic tapes are re-usable and can be overwritten.</p>
<p>EDIT: Any magnetic medium is re-writable by design (as the physical structure of the medium does not change, unlike in CDs and DVDs &#8212; your hard drive operates on the same principle, and it gets re-written and over-written thousands of times a day). The only way you could make a tape copy-protected is by introducing mechanical fail-safes into both the medium and the reproduction device &#8212; that is to say, while you have to bend over assward to make CDs re-writable, you have to bend over assward to make magnetic tapes NON-rewritable.</p>
<p>Good luck!</p>

